Now let me read a few sample CSV files to understand the data structure:
```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "head -3 data/OQMEA_train.csv && echo '---' && head -3 data/ILULR_train.csv && echo '---' && head -3 data/FDLOT_train.csv && echo '---' && head -3 data/RHHQD_train.csv"
  }
}
```

Windows environment. Let me use Python instead:
```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python -c \"import pandas as pd; df = pd.read_csv('data/OQMEA_train.csv'); print(df.shape); print(df.head(3)); print('---'); df2 = pd.read_csv('data/ILULR_train.csv'); print(df2.shape); print(df2.head(3))\""
  }
}
```

Good. Now let me look at a few more benchmarks to understand the diversity:
```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python -c \"import pandas as pd; import json; registry = json.load(open('data/benchmark_registry.json')); [print(k, pd.read_csv(f'data/{k}_train.csv').shape, 'cols:', list(pd.read_csv(f'data/{k}_train.csv').columns)) for k in registry]\""
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python -c \"import os; os.makedirs('code', exist_ok=True); os.makedirs('outputs', exist_ok=True); os.makedirs('report/images', exist_ok=True); print('dirs created')\""
  }
}
```

